CORE
dsb.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model reg:observe --mmio-weak --mmio-early-ack
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
the write has completed after the barrier: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
An inline-assembly ARM DSB (data synchronization barrier) is lowered to a
completion fence, so the write to reg has completed after it and the assertion
holds. Compare test.desc, where a DMB does not complete the write.
